=================================

1. TURN OFF POWER
   - Switch OFF the SMPS.
   - Unplug the power cord.
   - Make sure all PC components are installed properly.

2. CONNECT MOTHERBOARD
   - Cable: 24-pin ATX
   - Connect SMPS 24-pin ATX cable to motherboard 24-pin connector.
   - Cable: 4+4-pin EPS/CPU
   - Connect it to the motherboard 8-pin CPU power connector.

3. CONNECT GRAPHICS CARD
   - Cable: 6+2-pin PCIe
   - Connect the PCIe cable to the GPU power connector.
   - Some high-end GPUs use a 12VHPWR or 12V-2x6 connector.

4. CONNECT STORAGE DEVICES
   - Cable: SATA Power
   - Connect SATA power cable from SMPS to SATA SSD/HDD.
   - SATA data cable connects the drive to the motherboard.
   - SATA data cable does NOT come from the SMPS.

5. CHECK CONNECTIONS
   - Make sure all connectors are fully inserted.
   - Do not force any connector.
   - Keep cables away from cooling fans.

6. POWER ON
   - Connect the SMPS power cord.
   - Switch ON the SMPS.
   - Press the PC power button.




+----------------------+------------------+--------------------------+
| COMPONENT            | SMPS CABLE       | CONNECTOR                |
+----------------------+------------------+--------------------------+
| Motherboard          | 24-pin ATX       | 24-pin ATX               |
| CPU Power            | 4+4-pin EPS      | 8-pin CPU/EPS            |
| Graphics Card        | 6+2-pin PCIe     | 6/8-pin PCIe             |
| SATA SSD/HDD         | SATA Power       | SATA Power Connector     |

